  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRR-Team Scoping South Africa 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April and May 2022, the Province of KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, experienced heavy rainfall, resulting in the deaths of over 400 people and severe damages to (business) property, electricity, sanitation and public infrastructure. The impact on the South Durban Basin (SDB) has been particularly severe. The SDB is the second most concentrated industrial area in South Africa and makes a material contribution to regional supply chains across sub-Saharan Africa. To prevent further (future) damages to this Basin, the Municipality of eThekwini has requested technical support to assist the city of Durban with flood risk assessment and advice on flood risk mitigation measures.</narrative>
  </description>
